# Claude Code. Session state stays out; the SKILLS and slash-commands are project
# knowledge and are tracked -- they encode house rules (figure assembly, NRP deploys,
# paper voice) that every agent and machine needs, and lived untracked long enough that
# a skill's contents could not be shared or reviewed.
# Still ignored, deliberately:
#   worktrees/           -- 624 MB of checked-out git worktrees
#   settings.local.json  -- per-machine settings, personal by Claude Code convention
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/commands/

